From 06c9bf9a216c63acbb2009556e3870c09dcca2e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:50:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native ABC host adapter (Host implementation)

Port the ChronikBridge logic of chronik-cpp/chronik_bridge.cpp to the
native Host interface: block/tx conversion with spent coins from undo
data, disk offsets (first tx at data_pos + header size +
CompactSize(n_tx); undo after CompactSize(n_tx - 1); genesis undo 0),
chain view, raw header access, block/tx loading, legacy tx decoding
(DataError texts; trailing bytes accepted like TxMut::deser), spent-coin
lookup and uncaching, broadcast with the Rust error texts, and the fee
functions with the eCash-tier hysteresis.

The legacy transaction codec lives in the core (core/tx) so other hosts
with the same wire format can reuse it.

test_bitcoin gains chronik_native_abc_tests (21 cases), a port of the
bridgeprimitives/chronikbridge/bridgecompression expectations against
the adapter, used instead of the bridge tests in native builds. It
passes on the eCash tier (bitcoind) and on the V2 tier, where coinbase
outputs carry branches and the expectations are derived from the node's
own serialization.

Tier: eCash
